  "shared_context": [
    {
      "content": "For a fixed integer n>1, define F_n(x) = floor(n*x) - sum_{k=1}^n floor(k*x)/k for real x.",
      "kind": "definition",
      "label": "F_n"
    },
    {
      "content": "For a positive integer r, H_r = sum_{i=1}^r 1/i.",
      "kind": "notation",
      "label": "H_n"
    },
    {
      "content": "For a real number x, {x} = x - floor(x) denotes its fractional part.",
      "kind": "notation",
      "label": "fractional_part"
    }
  ],
  "strategy_summary": "Reduce by integer periodicity to the fractional part x in [0,1). Then split [0,1) into the intervals [m/n,(m+1)/n). The last interval is easy and gives the candidate value H_n-1 directly. On the earlier intervals, monotonicity reduces everything to the grid points m/n, and a residue-counting plus harmonic-sum estimate shows those grid values are strictly smaller than H_n-1. This identifies both the maximizing set and the maximum value.",
  "updated_at": "2026-03-29T00:09:26.890865Z"
}